3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Without the Licensor's prior written permission, you may NOT:

  (a) COPY any part of the Software into any other work. This is absolute and it is the central
      restriction of this license. It covers the Solidity contracts, the backend, the indexer, the
      frontend, the SDK, the scripts and the schemas, in whole or in part, verbatim or
      substantially derived, whether by copying source, by transcribing behaviour, or by
      translating it into another language or another chain;

  (b) DEPLOY the contracts, or any part or derivative of them, to any public network. Creating
      store contracts is done through the Canonical Factory and not by deploying your own copy;

  (c) OPERATE the Software, or a derivative of it, as a service for anyone other than yourself, or
      offer it to third parties, whether hosted, bundled, embedded, forked or otherwise, and
      whether or not for a fee;

  (d) REMOVE, obscure or alter this license, the SPDX identifiers, the copyright notices, or the
      provenance and canonicality mechanisms in the Software;

  (e) PRESENT a deployment that is not the Authorized Deployment as being the Authorized
      Deployment, or use the names, marks, domain or branding of the Licensor in a way likely to
      cause that confusion.

Reading the Software in order to understand it is permitted by Section 2(a). Reproducing what you
read is not.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. THE FACTORY IS THE AUTHORIZED WAY, AND IT IS FREE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You do not need to copy or deploy anything to have your own store.

The Canonical Factory creates a complete, independent store for you — its own store contract, its
own ERC20 store token, its own LicenseToken, its own governance and its own dividend distributor —
atomically, in one transaction, and the Licensor charges no fee for it. You pay only the network's
own gas.

Those contracts are yours to control. Nothing in this license restricts your use of a store you
created through the Canonical Factory, or of the store token it minted for you.

This is not a limitation dressed up as a feature. Provenance is what lets any Agent verify that a
store it is about to transact with is canonical rather than a convincing copy, and that guarantee
only exists if every canonical store comes from the same Factory. A deployed copy would be, by
construction, exactly the thing the provenance check is designed to reject.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. WHAT THIS LICENSE CANNOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Stated plainly, because a license that implied otherwise would be misleading:

Contract bytecode deployed to a public blockchain is readable and copyable by anyone, and this
license is a legal instrument rather than a technical control. It does not and cannot prevent
copying. It states what the Licensor permits and what the Licensor forbids; enforcement is a legal
matter, not a cryptographic one.

